215
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:15,200
Line). In the seventeen hundreds, a human named Richard Cantillon noticed something that everyone already knew but nobody

216
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:21,950
had written down: when you create new money, whoever gets it first benefits, and whoever gets it last pays.

217
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:29,500
On Wishonia, this is called "how money works." On Earth, it is taught as a niche economic theory, if it is taught at all.

218
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:35,080
Here's what it looks like: One. The Fed creates new money. Two.

219
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:39,960
Banks and government contractors receive it first. Three. They buy things at today's prices.

220
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:47,580
Four. Prices rise. Five. By the time the new money reaches your grocery store, everything costs more.

221
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:53,020
